Reason: in rooms busy with sleep and wake (the sand-block shaft, rm_a3h04: ~740 instances), instance_activate_region's
index of sleeping instances (patch 0062) was rebuilt on almost every call, ~1 ms each on the Wii: Samus's begin step
puts whole objects to sleep every frame (instance_deactivate_object) and wakes the ones near the view, and any create,
wake, sleep or destroy invalidated the index. The index is now kept current instead: an instance falling asleep is
added (its entry kept when its box hasn't moved since its last sleep), an awake one is passed over by its flag, and one
being freed has its entry cleared. Wakes go in room order through a list ordinal that rises along runner->instances (set
as an instance joins the list; the list only appends and compacts in order). The index is still rebuilt when the
instance list is replaced (room changes, persistence), when a sleeper's box moves (a dirty mark on an inactive live
instance), or when cleared entries pile up.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

